Voting Unit (Unit A):
Included: All stagehands and technicians employed by the Englert Civic Theatre, Inc., including carpenters, riggers, lighting technicians, audio technicians, fly rail operators, truck loaders, and other similar technical positions engaged in the loading in, operation and loading out of equipment used in connection with live entertainment events presented at the Englert Theatre; 

Excluded: All other employees including office clerical employees, and guards and supervisors as defined in the Act, as amended.

Also eligible to vote are all employees in the unit who have (a), within the year preceding the above eligibility date, worked at least five days and on two productions, regardless of the length of those days, or (b), within the two years preceding the above eligibility date, worked at least 15 days, regardless of the length of those days; and who have not been discharged for cause or quit voluntarily.

Included: All full-time and regular part-time Merchandisers; 
Excluded: Office and clerical employees, managers, and guards and supervisors as defined by the Act.

If a majority of valid ballots are cast for Teamsters Local 238, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to be included in the existing delivery and warehouse unit currently represented by Teamsters Local 238. If a majority of valid ballots are not cast for representation, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to remain unrepresented.

Including:  All full-time and regular part-time housekeeping, food and beverage, front desk, and maintenance employees employed by the Employer at the Hilton Garden Inn Dubuque Downtown, located in Dubuque, IA; 
Excluding: All office clerical employees, professional employees, Houlihan's employees, sales employees, accounting employees, and guards and supervisors as defined in the Act.

Other Permitted to vote:  The parties have agreed that the classifications of food & beverage supervisor, front desk supervisor, housekeeping supervisor, and lead engineer may vote in the election but their ballots will be challenged since their eligibility has not been resolved.  No decision has been made regarding whether the individuals in these classifications or groups are included in, or excluded from, the bargaining unit.  The eligibility or inclusion of these individuals will be resolved, if necessary, following the election.
